<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 245 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 245 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 245 million stg of unspecified late assistance.  </p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.4 BLN    1.35 BLN   1.2 BLN    1.2 BLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    463 MLN    913 MLN    930 MLN    1.175 BLN</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   =	     17 MLN*    17 MLN*    =</p>
<p> BAND 2  BANK BILLS   =	    101 MLN*   =	    =</p>
<p> BILLS/FRG TO FEB 10  463 MLN#   323 MLN   =	     =</p>
<p> UNSPECIFIED ASSISTANCE	    =	    =	     245 MLN</p>
<p>*INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p>#INTEREST RATE - 5-31/32 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
